[ti:PyTorch 2.9: More Portable Kernels, Smarter Compilation, and Wider Hardware Support]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: If you build C++ or CUDA extensions, run models across different GPUs, or care about long-context inference, PyTorch 2.9 has something aimed directly at you.
[00:00.00]Ava：如果你开发 C++ 或 CUDA 扩展、在不同 GPU 上运行模型，或关注长上下文推理，PyTorch 2.9 都有针对你的更新。
[00:12.19]Brian, what makes this release worth a close listen?
[00:12.19]Brian，这次发布为什么值得仔细听？
[00:16.57]Brian: It’s a broad release rather than one single headline feature.
[00:16.57]Brian：这次发布涵盖面很广，没有单一的主打功能。
[00:21.31]PyTorch 2.9 brings a more stable libtorch ABI, easier multi-GPU kernel programming through Symmetric Memory, finer control over graph breaks in torch.compile, and wider hardware packaging.
[00:21.31]PyTorch 2.9 带来了更稳定的 libtorch ABI、借助 Symmetric Memory 更方便地编写多 GPU 内核、对 torch.compile 图中断更细致的控制，以及覆盖更多硬件平台的安装包。
[00:35.90]It also has attention optimizations for Intel GPUs and X86 CPUs.
[00:35.90]它还优化了 Intel GPU 和 X86 CPU 上的注意力计算。
[00:41.21]Ava: Let’s start with the ABI piece.
[00:41.21]Ava：先说说 ABI。
[00:43.58]I’ve heard extension authors complain that a compiled extension can be tied too closely to one PyTorch version.
[00:43.58]我听扩展开发者抱怨过，编译好的扩展可能与某个 PyTorch 版本绑得太紧。
[00:52.06]Does 2.9 address that?
[00:52.06]2.9 解决了这个问题吗？
[00:54.09]Brian: That’s exactly the motivation. ABI means application binary interface.
[00:54.09]Brian：这正是改进的初衷。ABI 指应用程序二进制接口。
[00:59.56]PyTorch is building a stable ABI with C++ convenience wrappers, so you can build an extension with one torch version and run it with another.
[00:59.56]PyTorch 正在构建稳定的 ABI，并提供方便使用的 C++ 封装，让扩展可以用一个 torch 版本构建，再用另一个版本运行。
[01:10.58]In 2.9, that surface gets several new APIs.
[01:10.58]在 2.9 中，这部分新增了多个 API。
[01:14.29]Ava: What kind of APIs are we talking about?
[01:14.29]Ava：具体有哪些 API？
[01:17.37]Brian: There are device utilities, such as Device Guard and Stream, available through the stable accelerator header.
[01:17.37]Brian：稳定版加速器头文件提供了 Device Guard 和 Stream 等设备工具。
[01:26.99]The stable torch::stable::Tensor also gets a default constructor, is_cpu, scalar_type, and get_device_index.
[01:26.99]稳定的 torch::stable::Tensor 也新增了默认构造函数、is_cpu、scalar_type 和 get_device_index。
[01:36.52]And more stable ATen operations are exposed, including amax, narrow, dtype variants of new_empty and new_zeros, and pad.
[01:36.52]此外还开放了更多稳定的 ATen 操作，包括 amax、narrow、支持 dtype 的 new_empty 和 new_zeros 变体，以及 pad。
[01:47.46]Ava: So this is useful for people maintaining custom C++ or CUDA extensions, but it’s not a finished contract yet?
[01:47.46]Ava：所以这对维护自定义 C++ 或 CUDA 扩展的人很有用，但接口规范还没最终定下来？
[01:55.83]Brian: Right.
[01:55.83]Brian：对。
[01:56.29]The team enabled a libtorch-ABI wheel for Flash-Attention 3, which shows the direction.
[01:56.29]团队为 Flash-Attention 3 提供了 libtorch-ABI wheel，展示了发展方向。
[02:03.08]But the high-level C++ APIs are still in preview.
[02:03.08]但高级 C++ API 仍处于预览阶段。
[02:06.90]PyTorch says it’s continuing to expand the ABI surface, establish versioning, write more documentation, and make more custom kernels ABI stable.
[02:06.90]PyTorch 表示会继续扩展 ABI 接口、建立版本机制、完善文档，并让更多自定义内核支持稳定 ABI。
[02:18.47]Ava: That sounds like a compatibility layer being built piece by piece.
[02:18.47]Ava：听起来，这个兼容层正在逐步建成。
[02:23.13]Now, Symmetric Memory sounds more fundamental. What problem does it solve?
[02:23.13]接下来，Symmetric Memory 听起来更底层。它解决什么问题？
[02:28.71]Brian: It makes multi-GPU kernels easier to program across NVLinks and RDMA networks.
[02:28.71]Brian：它让开发者更容易编写跨 NVLink 和 RDMA 网络的多 GPU 内核。
[02:34.48]The key idea is that a GPU kernel can communicate while it computes.
[02:34.48]核心思路是让 GPU 内核在计算时也能通信。
[02:39.51]A kernel can issue puts and gets interleaved with computation instructions, so communication can be fused at a very small granularity.
[02:39.51]内核可以在计算指令之间穿插执行 put 和 get 操作，从而在很细的粒度上融合通信与计算。
[02:49.77]Ava: So instead of launching separate communication work and computation work, the kernel can coordinate both?
[02:49.77]Ava：也就是说，内核可以同时协调通信和计算，不必分别启动这两类任务？
[02:57.01]Brian: Exactly. There are three programming opportunities. First, in-kernel communication.
[02:57.01]Brian：没错。它提供了三种编程方式。第一种是内核内通信。
[03:03.44]Second, ultralow-latency remote access, where access can be one-sided and doesn’t wait for the remote GPU to issue a matching command.
[03:03.44]第二种是超低延迟远程访问：可以单边访问，无须等待远端 GPU 发出对应命令。
[03:13.83]Protocols such as RDMA and IB-GDA can provide direct memory access over the network.
[03:13.83]RDMA 和 IB-GDA 等协议可以通过网络提供直接内存访问。
[03:20.69]Ava: And the third opportunity is customization?
[03:20.69]Ava：第三种是自定义通信？
[03:24.30]Brian: Yes, customized communication patterns.
[03:24.30]Brian：对，自定义通信模式。
[03:26.88]Developers can write kernels tailored to an application’s communication needs.
[03:26.88]开发者可以根据应用的通信需求编写内核。
[03:32.03]The release also says it should be straightforward to add support for new data layouts, even when those layouts aren’t in standard libraries yet.
[03:32.03]发布说明还提到，即使标准库尚未支持某种数据布局，新增对它的支持也应该很直接。
[03:41.96]Ava: What is actually included in 2.9?
[03:41.96]Ava：2.9 具体包含哪些功能？
[03:45.26]Brian: Symmetric tensors can be allocated for remote direct access.
[03:45.26]Brian：可以分配对称张量，供远程直接访问。
[03:49.67]The currently supported backends are CUDA and NVSHMEM.
[03:49.67]目前支持的后端是 CUDA 和 NVSHMEM。
[03:53.64]There are also accelerated collectives using direct access, such as one-shot all-reduce, two-shot all-reduce, and multimem all-gather out.
[03:53.64]还有利用直接访问加速的集合通信操作，例如 one-shot all-reduce、two-shot all-reduce 和 multimem all-gather out。
[04:04.14]Ava: Those names are pretty specialized. Is there support for mixture-of-experts models too?
[04:04.14]Ava：这些名称很专业。混合专家模型也有相应支持吗？
[04:10.29]Brian: There is a nontraditional all-to-all-v path for MoE models, meaning mixture-of-experts models.
[04:10.29]Brian：有。MoE，也就是混合专家模型，可以使用一种非传统的 all-to-all-v 路径。
[04:17.51]The listed operations include all-to-all-v-dev, all-to-all-v-dev-2D, and an offset form for token combination.
[04:17.51]列出的操作包括 all-to-all-v-dev、all-to-all-v-dev-2D，以及用于合并 token 的 offset 形式。
[04:25.96]For custom multi-GPU kernels, there’s an NVSHMEM plugin for Triton, plus continued support for Async TP and generalization to other patterns.
[04:25.96]自定义多 GPU 内核可以使用面向 Triton 的 NVSHMEM 插件；Async TP 也继续得到支持，并扩展到其他模式。
[04:37.14]Ava: Where do developers access these operations?
[04:37.14]Ava：开发者从哪里调用这些操作？
[04:40.78]Brian: The Symmetric Memory operations are available under torch.ops.symm_mem.
[04:40.78]Brian：Symmetric Memory 操作可通过 torch.ops.symm_mem 使用。
[04:46.67]The article points users to the Symmetric Memory API documentation for details.
[04:46.67]文章建议用户查阅 Symmetric Memory API 文档，了解详细用法。
[04:53.23]It’s labeled API-Unstable, so users should expect the interface to evolve.
[04:53.23]它被标为 API-Unstable，接口预计还会变化。
[04:59.73]Ava: Let’s switch to torch.compile.
[04:59.73]Ava：接下来聊聊 torch.compile。
[05:02.13]Graph breaks can be useful during development, but sometimes I want them to fail loudly.
[05:02.13]开发时，图中断可能有用，但有时我希望它直接报错。
[05:09.18]What changed?
[05:09.18]这次有什么变化？
[05:10.57]Brian: PyTorch 2.9 adds torch._dynamo.error_on_graph_break().
[05:10.57]Brian：PyTorch 2.9 新增了 torch._dynamo.error_on_graph_break()。
[05:15.26]It’s a context manager and decorator.
[05:15.26]它既可用作上下文管理器，也可用作装饰器。
[05:18.48]You can mark regions of compiled code where torch.compile should error when it encounters a graph break, or resume instead.
[05:18.48]你可以标记编译代码中的特定区域，让 torch.compile 遇到图中断时选择报错或继续执行。
[05:29.52]Ava: How is that different from fullgraph?
[05:29.52]Ava：这和 fullgraph 有什么区别？
[05:32.29]Brian: The important difference is that error_on_graph_break can be toggled arbitrarily.
[05:32.29]Brian：关键区别是 error_on_graph_break 可以随时切换。
[05:37.89]With fullgraph, once you set it to true, you can’t set it back to false.
[05:37.89]而 fullgraph 一旦设为 true，就不能再改回 false。
[05:42.87]So the new option lets you choose stricter behavior only around the regions where you need it.
[05:42.87]因此，新选项让你只在需要的区域启用更严格的行为。
[05:49.73]Ava: That sounds useful for narrowing down a troublesome part of a model without forcing the whole program into one graph.
[05:49.73]Ava：这样就能定位模型中出问题的部分，而不用强制整个程序只用一张图。
[05:57.61]Brian: That’s the practical reading.
[05:57.61]Brian：实际使用时可以这么理解。
[05:59.61]The article describes it as expanding torch.compile’s graph-break options.
[05:59.61]文章将其描述为扩展了 torch.compile 处理图中断的选项。
[06:04.70]It also points to a tutorial for more details, so the exact usage patterns are best learned there.
[06:04.70]文章还提供了教程链接；具体用法最好参照教程。
[06:11.79]Ava: Packaging is another big theme. What does expanded wheel variant support mean for users?
[06:11.79]Ava：打包也是一大主题。扩展 wheel 变体支持对用户意味着什么？
[06:18.23]Brian: PyTorch is participating in the WheelNext initiative to improve the Python packaging ecosystem.
[06:18.23]Brian：PyTorch 正参与 WheelNext 计划，以改进 Python 打包生态。
[06:25.87]In 2.9.0, the wheel variant support matrix adds AMD ROCm, Intel XPU, and NVIDIA CUDA 13.
[06:25.87]在 2.9.0 中，wheel 变体支持矩阵新增了 AMD ROCm、Intel XPU 和 NVIDIA CUDA 13。
[06:32.95]These platforms get provider plugins that can detect platform attributes, including supported software and installed hardware.
[06:32.95]这些平台有相应的提供方插件，可检测支持的软件和已安装的硬件等平台属性。
[06:43.42]Ava: Is the support equally available on every operating system?
[06:43.42]Ava：所有操作系统都同样支持吗？
[06:47.88]Brian: No. NVIDIA CUDA wheels support Windows and Linux.
[06:47.88]Brian：不是。NVIDIA CUDA 的 wheel 支持 Windows 和 Linux。
[06:51.63]ROCm and XPU currently support Linux only.
[06:51.63]ROCm 和 XPU 目前仅支持 Linux。
[06:54.85]The article also stresses that this feature is experimental and based on a work-in-progress wheel variants proposal.
[06:54.85]文章还强调，这项功能仍处于实验阶段，依据的是尚未定稿的 wheel 变体提案。
[07:04.09]Ava: So users should treat it as an evolving installation path.
[07:04.09]Ava：所以用户应把它视为仍在演进的安装方式。
[07:08.55]Brian: Yes.
[07:08.55]Brian：是的。
[07:08.87]The article gives uv-based installation instructions for Linux x86, Linux aarch64, and macOS, and separate PowerShell instructions for Windows x86.
[07:08.87]文章提供了适用于 Linux x86、Linux aarch64 和 macOS 的 uv 安装说明，以及单独适用于 Windows x86 的 PowerShell 说明。
[07:20.94]The main point is that uv can select the appropriate torch wheel through the WheelNext installer URL.
[07:20.94]关键是 uv 可以通过 WheelNext 安装器地址选出合适的 torch wheel。
[07:29.58]Ava: Now, FlexAttention appears twice: once for Intel GPUs and once for X86 CPUs.
[07:29.58]Ava：FlexAttention 出现了两次：一次针对 Intel GPU，一次针对 x86 CPU。
[07:37.46]Let’s separate those.
[07:37.46]我们分别来说。
[07:39.99]Brian: On Intel GPUs, PyTorch 2.9 adds FlexAttention forward and backward support, aligned with common PyTorch GPU behavior.
[07:39.99]Brian：在 Intel GPU 上，PyTorch 2.9 新增了 FlexAttention 的前向和反向计算支持，与 PyTorch 在其他 GPU 上的常见行为保持一致。
[07:48.35]That gives developers more consistent and portable performance across different GPUs.
[07:48.35]这让开发者在不同 GPU 上获得更一致、可移植的性能。
[07:54.42]The article says code can be written once, and Hugging Face or Transformers workloads can use FlexAttention without code changes.
[07:54.42]文章称，代码只需编写一次，Hugging Face 或 Transformers 工作负载无需修改代码即可使用 FlexAttention。
[08:03.98]Ava: And the CPU feature is flash decoding?
[08:03.98]Ava：CPU 方面的新功能是 Flash Decoding 吗？
[08:07.40]Brian: Right.
[08:07.40]Brian：对。
[08:07.86]Flash decoding is a common LLM inference technique for speeding up attention and generation with long sequences.
[08:07.86]Flash Decoding 是一种常见的大语言模型推理技术，可加快长序列的注意力计算和生成。
[08:16.45]Before this release, the article says it existed only on the CUDA path.
[08:16.45]文章称，在此次发布前，它只支持 CUDA 路径。
[08:21.89]PyTorch 2.9 adds a FlexAttention-based optimization in the X86 CPU Inductor backend.
[08:21.89]PyTorch 2.9 在 X86 CPU Inductor 后端新增了基于 FlexAttention 的优化。
[08:28.68]Ava: How does that optimization create more parallel work?
[08:28.68]Ava：这种优化如何增加并行任务？
[08:32.75]Brian: It parallelizes the key-value sequence by partition and reduction.
[08:32.75]Brian：它通过分区和归约，对键值序列进行并行处理。
[08:37.26]That can improve CPU utilization when the original parallelism is insufficient.
[08:37.26]当原有并行度不足时，这可以提高 CPU 利用率。
[08:42.65]The examples given are small batch size, small head number, or short query sequence length combined with a long key-value sequence length.
[08:42.65]例如批量小、注意力头少，或查询序列短而键值序列长的情况。
[08:52.42]Ava: So the target is especially long-context decoding on CPUs?
[08:52.42]Ava：所以它尤其针对 CPU 上的长上下文解码？
[08:57.64]Brian: Yes.
[08:57.64]Brian：是的。
[08:57.92]The article says it’s expected to help during the LLM decoding phase, especially with long context length.
[08:57.92]文章预计它能改善大语言模型的解码阶段，尤其是上下文较长时。
[09:05.20]It doesn’t give a benchmark number, so we should describe the benefit as an intended optimization rather than quote a measured speedup.
[09:05.20]文章没有给出基准测试数据，因此应将其描述为预期的优化效果，而非实测加速。
[09:14.82]Ava: Good distinction. What about Arm?
[09:14.82]Ava：这个区别很重要。Arm 方面呢？
[09:18.17]Brian: PyTorch 2.9 delivers backend improvements and better test coverage on Arm.
[09:18.17]Brian：PyTorch 2.9 改进了 Arm 上的后端，并提高了测试覆盖率。
[09:23.31]In torch.compile mode, the TorchBench, HuggingFace, and TIMM test suites are faster than Eager mode, with results available on the PyTorch HUD Dashboard.
[09:23.31]在 torch.compile 模式下，TorchBench、HuggingFace 和 TIMM 测试套件都比 Eager 模式更快，结果可在 PyTorch HUD Dashboard 上查看。
[09:34.28]Ava: Are there operator-level changes too?
[09:34.28]Ava：算子层面也有变化吗？
[09:37.06]Brian: Yes.
[09:37.06]Brian：是的。
[09:37.37]Convolution, activation, and quantized operations on AArch64 were expanded and optimized for faster model execution.
[09:37.37]AArch64 上的卷积、激活和量化运算得到扩展与优化，可加快模型运行。
[09:46.53]Arm continuous-integration coverage was also broadened by adding AWS Graviton 4 instances based on Arm Neoverse V2.
[09:46.53]Arm 的持续集成测试也扩展到基于 Arm Neoverse V2 的 AWS Graviton 4 实例。
[09:55.96]Ava: And Linux aarch64 wheels are part of the release story as well?
[09:55.96]Ava：Linux aarch64 的 wheel 包也是本次发布的一部分吗？
[10:01.28]Brian: Yes.
[10:01.28]Brian：是的。
[10:01.56]The release highlights enablement of Linux aarch64 binary wheel builds across all supported CUDA versions.
[10:01.56]本次发布支持为所有受支持的 CUDA 版本构建 Linux aarch64 二进制 wheel 包。
[10:08.91]That should make installation easier for users on those Arm systems, although the article doesn’t enumerate the versions.
[10:08.91]这会让 Arm 系统用户更容易安装，不过文章没有列出具体版本。
[10:17.66]Ava: Before we wrap up, how large was this release effort?
[10:17.66]Ava：结束前再问一句，这次发布的规模有多大？
[10:22.33]Brian: Since PyTorch 2.8, the release includes three thousand two hundred sixteen commits from four hundred fifty-two contributors.
[10:22.33]Brian：自 PyTorch 2.8 以来，这次发布汇集了 452 位贡献者提交的 3216 个 commit。
[10:31.26]The team thanks the community and encourages users to try the features and report issues as 2.9 improves.
[10:31.26]团队感谢社区，并鼓励用户试用新功能、报告问题，帮助改进 2.9。
[10:39.17]Ava: Let me recap in three points.
[10:39.17]Ava：我用三点总结一下。
[10:40.61]First, the stable libtorch ABI and Symmetric Memory target extension authors and multi-GPU kernel developers.
[10:40.61]第一，稳定的 libtorch ABI 和 Symmetric Memory 面向扩展开发者及多 GPU 内核开发者。
[10:46.05]Second, torch.compile gets selective error-or-resume behavior for graph breaks.
[10:46.05]第二，torch.compile 可以针对特定图中断选择报错或继续执行。
[10:49.99]Third, hardware coverage expands through ROCm, XPU, CUDA 13, Intel GPUs, X86 CPUs, and Arm.
[10:49.99]第三，硬件支持扩展到 ROCm、XPU、CUDA 13、Intel GPU、X86 CPU 和 Arm。
[10:54.88]Brian: That’s the release in a nutshell.
[10:54.88]Brian：这就是本次发布的概要。
[10:57.27]The main limitation is maturity: several features are API-Unstable, the high-level C++ APIs are still in preview, and wheel variants are experimental.
[10:57.27]主要限制在于成熟度：多项功能仍标为 API-Unstable，高层 C++ API 仍处于预览阶段，wheel 变体也仍是实验性功能。
[11:08.12]So teams should test carefully and follow the documentation as these interfaces develop.
[11:08.12]因此，团队应仔细测试，并随着这些接口的发展关注文档。
[11:14.84]Ava: Thanks, Brian.
[11:14.84]Ava：谢谢你，Brian。
[11:15.83]For listeners, the three things to remember are: more stable extension compatibility, more flexible communication and compilation control, and broader hardware-specific performance work.
[11:15.83]听众记住三点就好：扩展兼容性更稳定，通信和编译控制更灵活，针对更多硬件开展了性能优化。
[11:29.32]Brian: And if you try PyTorch 2.9, report what breaks or improves.
[11:29.32]Brian：如果你试用了 PyTorch 2.9，也请反馈哪些地方出了问题、哪些地方有了改进。
[11:34.30]That feedback is part of how these APIs become dependable.
[11:34.30]这些反馈有助于让 API 更可靠。
[11:39.54]Ava: That’s all for today. Keep your kernels fast and your graph breaks intentional.
[11:39.54]Ava：今天就到这里。祝大家的内核运行飞快，计算图中断都在意料之中。
